    "verdict": "UNDERPOWERED",
    "derivation": "the smallest N whose Wilson 95% lower bound at p_hat = 0.95 exceeds 0.9. Wilson, never Wald: at p near 1 the normal approximation extends above 1.0 and its coverage collapses, which is exactly the regime a 0.95 claim is read in.",
    "mean_attributed_injections_per_firing_case": 0.0,
    "cases_with_any_injection": 0,
    "answerable_cases": 234,
    "implied_coverage_floor": null,
    "implied_coverage_floor_note": "the coverage this split would need at the MEASURED 0.00 injections per firing case to reach 139 attributed injections. Derived after the fact and reported; it never moves the floor.",
    "partial_coverage_is_a_pass": "PARTIAL COVERAGE AT HIGH PRECISION IS A PASS. Brief section 5.5 is precision-first -- 'the gate must be tuned for precision, with recall recovered by making the agent's explicit memory search tool excellent' -- and K1's wording carries no coverage term at all. A gate firing on 30% of queries at >= 0.95 precision MEETS K1's stated requirement. It is not a partial success and must not be reported as one.",
    "if_underpowered": "the precision number is reported as UNDERPOWERED -- not as a pass, and not as a failure. It means the held-out split could not certify the claim at this coverage, which is a statement about the INSTRUMENT, not about the gate."
  },
